Forward-landing pack for the planned M2 remote-vision seam (m2-design.md
section 2.4). build_vision still raises for every non-fake kind at M1, so
nothing wires this in yet; the call sites are documented in the module
docstring.

remotevision.py: stdlib-only (urllib) RemoteVision adapter hardened per the
W4C threat model - protocol echo + model/ms telemetry (A1), 1 MiB response
cap, frame-px cap before encode and MAX_DETECTIONS=64 truncation (A2),
https-unless-loopback/LAN-optin with no userinfo, query strings, redirects
or environment proxies (A3), exactly one HTTP attempt per pass (A4), token
read at call time from env and scrubbed from every error string (A6),
0 < timeout_s <= min(max_age_s, 60) and non-empty labels with errors naming
both config key and env var (A8), static artifact-safe name (A9).

tests/test_remotevision_acceptance.py: self-contained loopback mock driving
